{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>He sent</b> — He mentioned wild beasts first, because it was harsher than the plague of frogs. Or its meaning is: and the frogs had already corrupted them, like וַיָּרָם תּוֹלָעִים וַיָּבְאַשׁ (and it bred maggots and stank). And he did not mention the plague of lice, nor the plague of boils, nor the plague of darkness, nor the plague of hail, because people escaped and because the plague of blood was first of the plagues, so he mentioned it; also there is great need for water."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {0 "The phrase וירם תולעים ויבאש quotes Exodus 16:20 (the manna that bred worms and stank); the referent of 'he' in לא הזכיר is the psalmist. The word דם in מכת דם refers to the plague of blood (Exodus 7)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:15.268484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}